== S5. what the danger would look like: e-bar -> e-bar(1+c1*a) ==
  L := ln(1/ub_0) = 0.568615917914  (the pure numerator)
  e-bar(a) = e-bar_0*(1+c1*a)  =>  delta_A(a)*a = L - ln(1+c1*a):
  NOT a constant any more; the extra piece is -ln(1+c1*a) = O(1) at a=1.
  exact flip threshold:  c1*a > e^L - 1 = 1/ub_0 - 1 = 0.7658213176  (so c1 > 0.7658213176 at a=1)
     a        c1*a (c1=1)   delta_A*a (c1=1)   sign
  1.0      1.0           -0.124531262646     -
  0.7      0.7           0.0379876668517     +
  0.5      0.5           0.163150809806      +
  0.1      0.1           0.47330573811       +
  0.01     0.01          0.558665587061      +
  c1=0.5    -> sign flips for a > 1.5316426   (a=1: delta_A = 0.163150809806)
  c1=0.766  -> sign flips for a > 0.99976673   (a=1: delta_A = -0.000101184267923)
  c1=1.0    -> sign flips for a > 0.76582132   (a=1: delta_A = -0.124531262646)
  c1=3.0    -> sign flips for a > 0.25527377   (a=1: delta_A = -0.817678443206)
  => the danger, IF e-bar had an O(a) piece, is LIVE AT a=1 (where beta_1=0.147
     and delta_A*a=0.5686 are quoted): c1 > 0.7658 (a 77% lattice artifact in
     the animal constant) flips the sign.  c1 must be 0 EXACTLY, not 'small'.
     same threshold if the O(a) sits in u instead: numerator = L - ln(1+c*a).
== S6. the OTHER amplifiers (no 1/a, hence harmless) ==
  (i) c_f = beta/(2N) + O(beta^3) => u = beta/(2N^2) + O(beta^3):
      this shifts the NUMERATOR by O(u), relative size u/L = 0.0183193 ; margin L/u = 54.587128
      no 1/a factor => cannot flip the sign (numerator stays ~0.57 >> u=0.0104).
  (ii) C-hat (Z12=4) and C-bar (>=1):  numerator becomes ln(1/(C-hat*e-bar*C-bar))
      beta=1/12 (u=1/96) C-hat=1, C-bar=1  (C03 route) numerator=0.56861592    win beta<0.147152   sign=+
      beta=1/12 (u=1/96) C-hat=4, C-bar=1  (Z12 window) numerator=-0.81767844   win beta<0.0367879  sign=-
      beta=1/12 (u=1/96) C-hat=4, C-bar=e  (C02 pessim.) numerator=-1.8176784    win beta<0.0135335  sign=-
      beta=1/48 (u=1/384) C-hat=1, C-bar=1  (C03 route) numerator=1.9549103     win beta<0.147152   sign=+
      beta=1/48 (u=1/384) C-hat=4, C-bar=1  (Z12 window) numerator=0.56861592    win beta<0.0367879  sign=+
      beta=1/48 (u=1/384) C-hat=4, C-bar=e  (C02 pessim.) numerator=-0.43138408   win beta<0.0135335  sign=-
      => the numerator IS a pure number in every reading, but its SIGN is a
         beta-window statement, not an a-statement: beta=1/12 sits OUTSIDE the
         C-hat=4 window (beta_1^fix=3.679e-2 < 0.0833, Z12:161-162), that is why
         the C-hat=4 row at beta=1/12 is negative.  a-dependence: none anywhere.
         => delta_A = (pure number)/a in every in-window reading; no O(1) remainder.
== S7. verdict ==
  (1) e-bar = u-bar/u = e*D*C-bar = e*20*C-bar ; = 54.3656365692 with C-bar=1;
      8/e-bar = 0.1471517765 = beta_1 ; 8/0.147152 = 54.3656 : consistent [E]
  (2) D=20 combinatorial integer, C-bar pure (tree=animal identity), e constant
      => e-bar is a pure number, a-INDEPENDENT [T]
  (3) delta_A = (1/a)[ln(1/u) - ln e-bar] = ln(1/ub)/a , numerator pure [T]
      => delta_A is EXACTLY proportional to 1/a ; no O(1) remainder (S4: dev 0 to 50 dps)
  (4) f05's danger does NOT exist ; but it is not vacuous: c1 > 0.7658 at a=1 flips (S5).
  (5) residual a-dependence is only: 1/a^p conversions, L/a counting, e^{-cL/a}.
